{"issues":[{"expand":"renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations","id":"85411","self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/85411","key":"MC-269553","renderedFields":{"summary":null,"issuetype":null,"watches":null,"customfield_10070":null,"customfield_10061":"","created":"18/Mar/24 12:16 AM","customfield_10050":"","customfield_10051":null,"description":"<h3><a name=\"Thebug\"></a>The bug</h3>\n<p>Items with an empty NBT tag for enchantments (Enchantments:[]) do not upgrade to the new component system as expected. It'd be expected that they would get an enchantment_glint_override component tag, but this does not happen.</p>\n\n<p>Notably, items with the NBT tag (Enchantments:<span class=\"error\">[{}]</span>) <em>do</em> convert as expected, so it'd be expected that the other form would also do so.</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"Howtoreproduce\"></a>How to reproduce</h3>\n<p>A world containing \"phantom enchanted\" items is attached to this ticket.</p>\n<ol>\n\t<li>Open the attached world in 1.10.2 (in 1.11 to 1.20.4, the items won't visually appear enchanted due to a bug, but the NBT tag is still there)</li>\n\t<li>Verify that the items look enchanted</li>\n\t<li>Open the attached world in the latest 1.20.5 snapshot</li>\n\t<li>Verify that not only do they not look enchanted, but that the empty enchantment tag is completely gone, and these items are now identical to normal unenchanted items</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n<h3><a name=\"Expectedresults\"></a>Expected results</h3>\n<p>These items would keep their enchantment glint in 1.20.5+ by converting to the new enchantment_glint_override component.</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"Actualresults\"></a>Actual results</h3>\n<p>They do not.</p>","customfield_10054":null,"fixVersions":null,"customfield_10055":null,"resolution":null,"customfield_10047":"18/Mar/24 12:53 PM","customfield_10048":null,"labels":null,"customfield_10049":null,"attachment":[{"self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachmen